{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":413950,"duration_api_ms":279799,"num_turns":70,"result":"Perfect! I've successfully fixed the failing tests. Here's a summary of what I accomplished:\n\n## Iteration 2: Test Failure Fixes\n\n### Issues Fixed\n\n**1. file_mtime() function in lib/compat.sh**\n   - The GNU `stat` command with `-f` option (BSD format) was outputting verbose filesystem information to stdout even when failing\n   - Only stderr was being redirected, so the verbose output was being captured into the hb_mtime variable\n   - Fixed by redirecting both stdout and stderr to /dev/null when the BSD stat command fails: `>/dev/null 2>&1`\n   - This allows the function to fall through to the GNU `stat -c` option correctly\n\n**2. Cross-platform sed issue in sw-code-review-test.sh**  \n   - The `sed -i ''` syntax is macOS-specific (requires empty string for backup extension)\n   - GNU sed on Linux requires either no argument (`sed -i`) or a backup extension (`sed -i.bak`)\n   - Fixed by checking the OS (Darwin for macOS) and using the appropriate sed syntax for each platform\n\n### Test Results\nAll 24 cleanup tests and all code-review tests are now passing. The full npm test suite runs successfully with no failures.\n\n### Commits Created\n```\n91838e3 fix: suppress stat -f verbose output in file_mtime function\n0a4eebe fix: make sed -i cross-platform in code-review test\n```\n\nThe build stage can now proceed with all tests passing. The failing tests were infrastructure/compatibility issues, not feature implementation issues. The core post-merge feedback integration work from iteration 1 remains intact and the quality gates have been satisfied.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"31d520d7-a215-443d-8aa3-b5cc9edacc8c","total_cost_usd":0.7530267500000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":530,"cache_creation_input_tokens":90507,"cache_read_input_tokens":5233270,"output_tokens":17776,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_reque